  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything, because the premise looks wrong. `contracts/consumers/analytics-ingest__OrderPlaced.json` shows that `analytics-ingest` (deployed version 3) lists `channel` as a required field of `OrderPlaced`:\n\n```\n\"channel\": \"enum:web|store|marketplace\"\n```\n\nIf I remove `channel` from the event, that consumer would probably break. `scripts/verify-contracts.mjs` also checks this contract.\n\nInside this repo, `channel` is only used in the event payload (`src/core/events.ts`), the order model and validation (`src/core/order.ts`), and request parsing (`src/api/requestParsing.ts`). It also appears in tests, docs and the contract script.\n\nHow do you want to proceed?\n1. **Check first.** If analytics-ingest has stopped using `channel` and its contract has been updated or retired, I'll remove the field everywhere. That includes `POST /orders` input, validation, tests, README, CLAUDE.md and the contract files.\n2. **Remove it from the order model only.** The event would keep `channel`, perhaps with a fixed value. That seems awkward, since the event is built from the order.\n3. **Leave it as is** until analytics-ingest drops the requirement.\n\nRemoving it from `POST /orders` input is also a breaking API change for any caller that sends `channel`. Do you want that included?",
